From: postmarketOS rhodep port
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: pd_mapper: add sm6375

sm6375 is missing from the match table, so qcom_pd_mapper never probes on it
and nothing provides the service registry. The module loads and then sits
there: no entry under /sys/bus/platform/drivers/qcom_pd_mapper, nothing in the
log, no domains advertised.

Firmware on a Motorola Moto G82 5G (SM6375) says what that costs, in its own
words. Among the strings in the modem image:

	Diag_LSM.c:servreg_get_local_domain() returned null

so the modem's diagnostic subsystem asks for its protection domain, is told
there is none, and does not start. Which matches what is seen from the other
side: the modem advertises twelve glink channels and none of them is a diag
channel, and opening DIAG, DIAG_CNTL or DIAG_DATA from the AP never completes,
because nothing on the modem owns them.

sm6375 has mpss, adsp and cdsp, the same three as sm6115, so it takes the same
domain set.
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_pd_mapper.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_pd_mapper.c
@@ -615,6 +615,7 @@
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm4250", .data = sm6115_domains, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6115", .data = sm6115_domains, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6350", .data = sm6350_domains, },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm6375", .data = sm6115_domains, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm7150", .data = sm7150_domains, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm7225", .data = sm6350_domains, },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm7325", .data = sc7280_domains, },
